export anchor Overview:
    overview:
        Piton is loosely typed with optional type constraints.

    types:
        All the usual suspects are present.

        string: A unicode string
        number: All-encompassing numeric type; int or float.
        boolean: true or false
        null: The absence of a value
        list: A list of values. Value types can be mixed as long as it’s not constrained by a type annotation.
        dictionary: A dictionary of key-value pairs. Key types must be strings, and value types can be mixed as long as it’s not constrained by a type annotation.
        anchor: The core structural building block of Piton. Don't worry, there's a whole section on this.
